title: The Bielefeld Agreement
subtitle: The government offers the Ruhr terms.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_ruhr = 1 and crisis_time = 3
max-visits: 1
priority: 5
on-arrival: {!
// a week of fighting: Watter's troops arrive, and the front gives where it is thin
Q.e20_ruhr_watter += Q.kapp_outcome == 3 ? 3 : 10;
var lost = Math.max(0, Math.round((Q.e20_ruhr_watter - Q.e20_ruhr_men * 0.6) / 6));
if (Q.e20_ruhr_dug) { lost = Math.floor(lost / 2); }
Q.e20_ruhr_towns = Math.max(0, Q.e20_ruhr_towns - lost);
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Towns held: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_towns;
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
!}

= The Bielefeld Agreement

[? if kapp_outcome != 2 : On 24 March, at Bielefeld, the Prussian commissioner Carl Severing meets the Ruhr's parties, unions and councils. His terms: the Reichswehr stays out, the putschists will be punished, local workers' defence units may remain, and the Red Army hands in its weapons. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 2 : General von Watter sends an officer to Hagen under a white flag. He offers an amnesty for the rank and file if every rifle is handed in within a week. ?]

The USPD council in Hagen is ready to sign. The council in Essen, where our comrades are strong, says the generals have never kept a promise. [? if kapp_outcome = 3 : Legien's government has promised to hold Watter to the terms. ?]

- @accept: Sign, and hand in the guns in good order.
- @keep_arms: Sign, and keep the best rifles hidden.
- @reject: Reject the terms and hold the Lippe.
- @soviet: Proclaim a Ruhr republic of councils.

@accept
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Thousands of men go home. It depends on Watter keeping his word.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any agreement with the government.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.bielefeld = 1;
Q.e20_ruhr_men = Math.max(5, Q.e20_ruhr_men - 20);
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_men + ',000 men';
!}

Our delegates sign beside the Hagen council. Columns of miners march to the collection points and stack their rifles. On the Lippe some units refuse.

@keep_arms
subtitle: Some men go home. The machine guns go down the pits.
on-arrival: {!
Q.bielefeld = 3;
Q.e20_ruhr_men = Math.max(5, Q.e20_ruhr_men - 10);
Q.red_guards_arms += 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_men + ',000 men';
!}

We sign. The councils keep meeting under new names, in the back rooms of the co-operatives.

@reject
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Red Army stays whole. Berlin will send Watter more troops.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.bielefeld = 2;
Q.e20_ruhr_watter += 10;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
!}

The Essen council tears up the agreement. Its commanders tell the men at the front that the generals are afraid of them.

@soviet
subtitle: The most radical pits will rally to it. The generals will have their excuse.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.bielefeld = 4;
Q.e20_ruhr_watter += 15;
Q.e20_ruhr_men += 5;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 10;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 3;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_men + ',000 men';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
!}

In Mülheim and Duisburg the councils depose the mayors and proclaim a republic of workers' councils. The Hagen council disowns them the same afternoon.
